{%- comment -%}
  Blog stories (Figma "Stories of Transformation"): an eyebrow, a heading and a "View journal" link
  above story cards. With 4 stories on "Automatic": the Figma mosaic. Large screens: a wide featured
  story, two stories stacked in the middle, a tall story at the end (Layout "Featured right" mirrors
  it). Tablets: the featured story full width, two side by side, the fourth full width. Phones (Figma
  mobile): the featured story full width, then two stacked stories next to the tall one. With more than
  4 stories, or once a story picks its own Shape, a free grid takes over (see grid_mode below).

  Where the stories come from (both work together):
  - Blog: the newest articles of the chosen blog fill the places automatically.
  - Story blocks (4 by default, drag to reorder, block 1 = the featured card): each block is one place.
    Pick an Article there to pin that article to the place; leave it empty and the place takes the next
    newest blog article that isn't pinned elsewhere (so nothing shows twice). Custom image and Category
    work for pinned and automatic stories alike.
  - No blocks at all: the 4 newest blog articles, newest first.

  A place with no article: "Fill empty places" on = the other cards close the gap (the mosaic becomes
  equal columns); off = the place stays empty. No card at all on the live store = no section.

  Highlight color: the eyebrow, the italic words of the heading and the categories. Empty = the color
  scheme's "Links and highlights" color (the homepage saves the Figma gold).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign stories_blog = section.settings.blog
  assign scheme_id = section.settings.color_scheme.id | default: 'scheme-1'
  assign fill_empty = section.settings.fill_empty

  # Pinned articles (chosen in a Story block), as "|handle|" marks in one string, so the automatic
  # fill can skip them: contains on "|my-post|" can't match a different post by accident
  assign pinned = '|'
  assign pinned_count = 0
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.settings.article != blank
      assign pinned = pinned | append: block.settings.article.handle | append: '|'
      assign pinned_count = pinned_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor
  # Places = Story blocks, or 4 when there are none.
  assign place_total = section.blocks.size
  if place_total == 0
    assign place_total = 4
  endif

  # The blog's articles that are not pinned, as positions in the blog (newest first). The blog is read
  # one time here; each place below only takes the next position from this list.
  assign free_positions = ''
  if stories_blog != blank
    for candidate in stories_blog.articles limit: 50
      assign mark = '|' | append: candidate.handle | append: '|'
      unless pinned contains mark
        assign free_positions = free_positions | append: forloop.index0 | append: ','
      endunless
    endfor
  endif
  assign free_list = free_positions | split: ','

  # The story of each place, decided one time: 'pin' (the block's article), a position in the blog,
  # or 'none'. Cards = the places that get an article.
  assign picks = ''
  assign next_free = 0
  assign card_count = 0
  for place in (1..place_total)
    assign block_index = place | minus: 1
    assign pick = 'none'
    if section.blocks[block_index].settings.article != blank
      assign pick = 'pin'
    elsif next_free < free_list.size
      assign pick = free_list[next_free]
      assign next_free = next_free | plus: 1
    endif
    if pick != 'none'
      assign card_count = card_count | plus: 1
    endif
    assign picks = picks | append: pick | append: ','
  endfor
  assign pick_list = picks | split: ','

  # Empty places (no article):
  # - "Fill empty places" on: they are not shown; the other cards close the gap.
  # - Off: they keep their space (an invisible card; a placeholder in the theme editor).
  # - No card at all: the theme editor shows a placeholder in every place, the live store no section.
  # So the editor shows the same layout as the live store.
  assign keep_place = true
  if fill_empty
    assign keep_place = false
  endif
  if request.design_mode and card_count == 0
    assign keep_place = true
  endif
  assign column_count = place_total
  if keep_place == false
    assign column_count = card_count
  endif

  # View journal: the link setting, else the chosen blog, else the blog of the first pinned article.
  # The article URL is cut after the blog handle (/blogs/<blog>/<article> → /blogs/<blog>), so a
  # language prefix such as /fr stays.
  assign view_all_url = section.settings.link
  if view_all_url == blank and stories_blog != blank
    assign view_all_url = stories_blog.url
  endif
  if view_all_url == blank
    for block in section.blocks
      if block.settings.article != blank
        assign url_parts = block.settings.article.url | split: '/'
        assign previous_part = ''
        for part in url_parts
          if part == blank
            continue
          endif
          assign view_all_url = view_all_url | append: '/' | append: part
          if previous_part == 'blogs'
            break
          endif
          assign previous_part = part
        endfor
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign animation = section.settings.animation
  if section.index == 1
    assign animation = 'none'
  endif

  # Card shapes: as long as every Story block is on "Automatic", the Figma mosaic is used (Layout
  # setting). As soon as one block picks its own shape, the grid switches to "custom": a 12-column grid
  # where each card takes its shape's space and the cards pack in order, filling gaps.
  # More than 4 stories don't fit the 4-place mosaic either, so they use the custom grid too.
  # The mosaic needs 4 places. With fewer (fewer than 4 Story blocks, or empty places that are not
  # kept), the cards show as equal columns, so the layout has no holes.
  assign grid_mode = section.settings.layout
  if section.blocks.size > 4
    assign grid_mode = 'custom'
  endif
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.settings.size != blank and block.settings.size != 'auto'
      assign grid_mode = 'custom'
      break
    endif
  endfor
  if grid_mode != 'custom' and column_count < 4
    assign grid_mode = 'equal'
  endif

  # Image sizes: the content width on large screens (Section width), in px; 0 = no limit
  assign width_cap = 0
  case section.settings.section_width
    when 'narrow'
      assign width_cap = 1200
    when 'wide'
      assign width_cap = settings.max_page_width | remove: 'rem' | times: 16 | round
  endcase
  assign equal_columns = column_count | at_least: 1
  assign equal_share = 100 | divided_by: equal_columns
  assign priority_done = false
  assign first_card_done = false
-%}

{%- if card_count > 0 or request.design_mode -%}
  <div
    class="blog-stories full-width section-width--{{ section.settings.section_width | default: 'wide' }} color-{{ scheme_id }}"
    style="{% if section.settings.highlight_color != blank %}--color-accent: {{ section.settings.highlight_color }}; {% endif %}--section-padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px; --section-padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;"
  >
    <div class="blog-stories__inner">
      <div class="blog-stories__header">
        <div class="blog-stories__titles">
          {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
            <p class="eyebrow blog-stories__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
            <h2 class="blog-stories__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        {%- if section.settings.link_label != blank and view_all_url != blank -%}
          <a class="button button--text blog-stories__view-all" href="{{ view_all_url }}">
            {{- section.settings.link_label | escape -}}
            <span class="blog-stories__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{{ 'icon-arrow.svg' | inline_asset_content }}</span>
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <animate-on-scroll>
        <ul
          class="blog-stories__grid blog-stories__grid--{{ grid_mode }}"
          role="list"
          {% if grid_mode == 'equal' %}
            style="--cards: {{ equal_columns }};"
          {% endif %}
          {% if animation != 'none' %}
            data-animate="{{ animation }}"
          {% endif %}
        >
          {%- for place in (1..place_total) -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign block_index = place | minus: 1
              assign block = section.blocks[block_index]

              # The story picked for this place above: the pinned article, or the blog article at the
              # picked position (offset + limit 1 reads that one article only)
              assign pick = pick_list[block_index]
              assign story = nil
              case pick
                when 'pin'
                  assign story = block.settings.article
                when 'none'
                  assign story = nil
                else
                  assign pick_position = pick | plus: 0
                  for candidate in stories_blog.articles offset: pick_position limit: 1
                    assign story = candidate
                  endfor
              endcase

              # An empty place: skipped, or kept (invisible on the live store, a placeholder in the editor)
              if story == blank and keep_place == false
                continue
              endif
              assign show_placeholder = false
              if story == blank and request.design_mode
                assign show_placeholder = true
              endif

              # Pill: the block's own text; with no blocks, "Featured story" on the first card
              assign pill = block.settings.pill_label
              if section.blocks.size == 0 and place == 1
                assign pill = 'sections.blog_stories.featured' | t
              endif

              # "Automatic" shape. In the mosaic: 1 featured, 4 portrait, the others small (the mosaic
              # CSS places them). In the custom grid: the repeating pattern Featured, Small, Portrait,
              # Small, which packs into the same mosaic band every 4 stories, so 8 or 12 stories still
              # look designed. In equal columns: the first card shown is featured (pill, excerpt, an H2
              # title, see the CSS), the others small, so the cards in the row look the same.
              assign card_size = block.settings.size
              if card_size == blank or card_size == 'auto'
                if grid_mode == 'equal'
                  assign card_size = 'small'
                  if first_card_done == false
                    assign card_size = 'featured'
                  endif
                elsif grid_mode == 'custom'
                  assign pattern_place = block_index | modulo: 4
                  case pattern_place
                    when 0
                      assign card_size = 'featured'
                    when 2
                      assign card_size = 'portrait'
                    else
                      assign card_size = 'small'
                  endcase
                else
                  case place
                    when 1
                      assign card_size = 'featured'
                    when 4
                      assign card_size = 'portrait'
                    else
                      assign card_size = 'small'
                  endcase
                endif
              endif

              # Image width in % of the screen: large (≥ 1200px) / tablets / phones, from the card's
              # place in the layout (the CSS below)
              case grid_mode
                when 'equal'
                  assign share_large = equal_share
                  assign share_tablet = equal_share
                  assign share_phone = 100
                when 'custom'
                  case card_size
                    when 'featured'
                      assign share_large = 50
                      assign share_tablet = 50
                      assign share_phone = 100
                    when 'landscape'
                      assign share_large = 50
                      assign share_tablet = 100
                      assign share_phone = 100
                    else
                      assign share_large = 25
                      assign share_tablet = 50
                      assign share_phone = 50
                  endcase
                else
                  case place
                    when 1
                      assign share_large = 53
                      assign share_tablet = 100
                      assign share_phone = 100
                    when 4
                      assign share_large = 22
                      assign share_tablet = 100
                      assign share_phone = 45
                    else
                      assign share_large = 27
                      assign share_tablet = 50
                      assign share_phone = 56
                  endcase
              endcase
              if width_cap > 0
                assign cap_px = width_cap | times: share_large | divided_by: 100
                assign large_size = 'min(' | append: share_large | append: 'vw, ' | append: cap_px | append: 'px)'
              else
                assign large_size = share_large | append: 'vw'
              endif
              assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 1200px) ' | append: large_size | append: ', (min-width: 750px) ' | append: share_tablet | append: 'vw, ' | append: share_phone | append: 'vw'

              # fetchpriority=high: only the first card with a photo (custom image or article image),
              # only in the first section
              assign card_priority = false
              if section.index == 1 and priority_done == false
                if block.settings.image != blank or story.image != blank
                  assign card_priority = true
                  assign priority_done = true
                endif
              endif
              assign first_card_done = true

              # Zoom point in % (x, y): one of the 9 arrow positions, or blank = the image's focal point
              assign zoom_x = blank
              assign zoom_y = blank
              case block.settings.zoom_point
                when 'top-left'
                  assign zoom_x = 15
                  assign zoom_y = 15
                when 'top'
                  assign zoom_x = 50
                  assign zoom_y = 15
                when 'top-right'
                  assign zoom_x = 85
                  assign zoom_y = 15
                when 'left'
                  assign zoom_x = 15
                  assign zoom_y = 50
                when 'center'
                  assign zoom_x = 50
                  assign zoom_y = 50
                when 'right'
                  assign zoom_x = 85
                  assign zoom_y = 50
                when 'bottom-left'
                  assign zoom_x = 15
                  assign zoom_y = 85
                when 'bottom'
                  assign zoom_x = 50
                  assign zoom_y = 85
                when 'bottom-right'
                  assign zoom_x = 85
                  assign zoom_y = 85
              endcase
            -%}
            {% render 'story-card',
              article: story,
              image: block.settings.image,
              category: block.settings.category,
              pill_label: pill,
              size: card_size,
              sizes: card_sizes,
              priority: card_priority,
              keep_place: keep_place,
              placeholder: show_placeholder,
              zoom: block.settings.zoom,
              zoom_x: zoom_x,
              zoom_y: zoom_y,
              attributes: block.shopify_attributes
            %}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      </animate-on-scroll>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .blog-stories {
    padding-block: var(--section-padding-top) var(--section-padding-bottom);
  }

  .blog-stories__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 1.5rem + 3vw, 6rem);
    inline-size: min(
      calc(var(--section-width, var(--page-width)) - var(--page-margin) * 2),
      calc(100% - var(--page-margin) * 2)
    );
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .blog-stories__header {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .blog-stories__titles {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .blog-stories__eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .blog-stories__heading {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size-display);
  }

  /* "*Stories of* Transformation": italic words in the highlight color, not slanted */
  .blog-stories__heading em {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .blog-stories__view-all {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 70%, var(--color-background));
  }

  .blog-stories__arrow svg {
    inline-size: 1em;
    block-size: auto;
  }

  .blog-stories__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .blog-stories__card {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    min-block-size: 18rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background-color: #1f1f1f;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  /* "Fill empty places" off: a place with no article keeps its space in the layout */
  .blog-stories__card--empty {
    visibility: hidden;
  }

  /*
    Phones (Figma mobile): the featured card full width, then two stacked cards next to the tall card
    (Featured right: the tall card on the left). Columns about 5 : 4. Custom shapes: 2 columns.
  */
  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    /*
      Figma mobile: the eyebrow on its own line, then the heading with the link next to its last line.
      The titles box is skipped (display: contents) so the eyebrow can take the full width.
    */
    .blog-stories__header {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
      align-items: end;
    }

    .blog-stories__titles {
      display: contents;
    }

    .blog-stories__eyebrow {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }

    /* The 50px corners of large cards make the short phone cards look like pills */
    .blog-stories__card {
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    }

    .blog-stories__heading {
      font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1rem + 2.5vw, 2.5rem);
    }

    .blog-stories__view-all {
      flex: none;
    }

    .blog-stories__grid {
      gap: var(--space-sm);
    }

    .blog-stories__grid--featured-left {
      grid-template-columns: 5fr 4fr;
    }

    .blog-stories__grid--featured-right {
      grid-template-columns: 4fr 5fr;
    }

    :is(.blog-stories__grid--featured-left, .blog-stories__grid--featured-right) {
      grid-template-rows: auto repeat(2, minmax(6.5rem, auto));
    }

    .blog-stories__grid--custom {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      grid-auto-rows: minmax(6.5rem, auto);
      grid-auto-flow: row dense;
    }

    :is(.blog-stories__grid--featured-left, .blog-stories__grid--featured-right, .blog-stories__grid--custom) .blog-stories__card {
      min-block-size: 0;
    }

    :is(.blog-stories__grid--featured-left, .blog-stories__grid--featured-right) .blog-stories__card:nth-child(1),
    .blog-stories__grid--custom .blog-stories__card--featured {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      min-block-size: 15rem;
    }

    .blog-stories__grid--featured-left .blog-stories__card:nth-child(2) { grid-area: 2 / 1; }
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-left .blog-stories__card:nth-child(3) { grid-area: 3 / 1; }
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-left .blog-stories__card:nth-child(4) { grid-area: 2 / 2 / 4 / 3; }
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-right .blog-stories__card:nth-child(2) { grid-area: 2 / 2; }
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-right .blog-stories__card:nth-child(3) { grid-area: 3 / 2; }
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-right .blog-stories__card:nth-child(4) { grid-area: 2 / 1 / 4 / 2; }

    .blog-stories__grid--custom .blog-stories__card--landscape { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .blog-stories__grid--custom .blog-stories__card--portrait { grid-row: span 2; }

    /* The small and tall cards on phones: less padding, smaller text (not Featured, not Landscape) */
    :is(.blog-stories__grid--featured-left, .blog-stories__grid--featured-right, .blog-stories__grid--custom) .blog-stories__card:not(.blog-stories__card--featured, .blog-stories__card--landscape) .blog-stories__text {
      gap: 0.25rem;
      padding: 0.75rem 0.875rem;
    }

    :is(.blog-stories__grid--featured-left, .blog-stories__grid--featured-right, .blog-stories__grid--custom) .blog-stories__card:not(.blog-stories__card--featured, .blog-stories__card--landscape) .blog-stories__category {
      font-size: 0.625rem;
    }

    :is(.blog-stories__grid--featured-left, .blog-stories__grid--featured-right, .blog-stories__grid--custom) .blog-stories__card:not(.blog-stories__card--featured, .blog-stories__card--landscape) .blog-stories__title {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

  }

  /* Tablets: the featured card full width, cards 2 and 3 side by side, card 4 full width */
  @media (min-width: 750px) and (max-width: 1199px) {
    .blog-stories__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    :is(.blog-stories__grid--featured-left, .blog-stories__grid--featured-right) .blog-stories__card:nth-child(1) {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      min-block-size: 24rem;
    }

    :is(.blog-stories__grid--featured-left, .blog-stories__grid--featured-right) .blog-stories__card:nth-child(4) {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }

    /* Custom shapes on tablets: two columns, cards pack in order and fill gaps */
    .blog-stories__grid--custom {
      grid-auto-flow: row dense;
    }

    .blog-stories__grid--custom .blog-stories__card--landscape {
      grid-column: span 2;
    }

    .blog-stories__grid--custom :is(.blog-stories__card--featured, .blog-stories__card--portrait) {
      grid-row: span 2;
    }
  }

  /*
    Large screens: the mosaic (Figma, 1920px): columns about 10 : 5 : 4, two equal rows.
    Card 1 (featured) = the wide left column, both rows; cards 2 and 3 = middle column, one row each;
    card 4 = right column, both rows.
  */
  @media (min-width: 1200px) {
    .blog-stories__grid {
      /*
        Each row is at least 15-24rem (growing with the screen) and grows further if a card's text needs
        it (auto), so a card can never be taller than its row and run into the one below.
      */
      grid-template-rows: repeat(2, minmax(clamp(15rem, 17vw, 24rem), auto));
    }

    .blog-stories__card {
      min-block-size: 0;
    }

    /* Featured left (Figma): wide featured | 2 stacked | tall */
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-left {
      grid-template-columns: 10fr 5fr 4fr;
    }

    .blog-stories__grid--featured-left .blog-stories__card:nth-child(1) { grid-area: 1 / 1 / 3 / 2; }
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-left .blog-stories__card:nth-child(2) { grid-area: 1 / 2 / 2 / 3; }
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-left .blog-stories__card:nth-child(3) { grid-area: 2 / 2 / 3 / 3; }
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-left .blog-stories__card:nth-child(4) { grid-area: 1 / 3 / 3 / 4; }

    /* Featured right (mirrored): tall | 2 stacked | wide featured */
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-right {
      grid-template-columns: 4fr 5fr 10fr;
    }

    .blog-stories__grid--featured-right .blog-stories__card:nth-child(1) { grid-area: 1 / 3 / 3 / 4; }
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-right .blog-stories__card:nth-child(2) { grid-area: 1 / 2 / 2 / 3; }
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-right .blog-stories__card:nth-child(3) { grid-area: 2 / 2 / 3 / 3; }
    .blog-stories__grid--featured-right .blog-stories__card:nth-child(4) { grid-area: 1 / 1 / 3 / 2; }

    /*
      Custom (a Story block picked its own shape): 12 columns, rows as tall as the mosaic's rows, as many
      rows as needed. Featured = half the width x 2 rows, Landscape = half x 1, Small = a quarter x 1,
      Portrait = a quarter x 2. "dense" lets a later small card fill a hole left earlier, so e.g.
      Featured, Small, Portrait, Small rebuilds the Figma mosaic.
    */
    .blog-stories__grid--custom {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr));
      grid-template-rows: none;
      grid-auto-rows: minmax(clamp(15rem, 17vw, 24rem), auto);
      grid-auto-flow: row dense;
    }

    .blog-stories__grid--custom .blog-stories__card--featured { grid-column: span 6; grid-row: span 2; }
    .blog-stories__grid--custom .blog-stories__card--landscape { grid-column: span 6; }
    .blog-stories__grid--custom .blog-stories__card--small { grid-column: span 3; }
    .blog-stories__grid--custom .blog-stories__card--portrait { grid-column: span 3; grid-row: span 2; }
  }

  /* Equal columns ("Fill empty places" with fewer than 4 cards): one row from tablets up */
  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .blog-stories__grid--equal {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--cards, 1), minmax(0, 1fr));
      grid-template-rows: minmax(clamp(18rem, 26vw, 30rem), auto);
    }
  }

  /* Photo fills the card; a dark fade from the bottom keeps the white text readable */
  .blog-stories__media {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: -1;
  }

  .blog-stories__media .image,
  .blog-stories__placeholder {
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
  }

  /*
    Hover (Figma hover state): the photo slowly zooms in (Story block "Zoom amount", 112% by default;
    100% = none) towards its zoom point: the block's own position, else the image's focal point set in
    the image picker, else the centre. The text stays still. Only on screens with a real pointer (a tap
    must not leave the zoom on) and without reduced motion; keyboard focus zooms the same way.
  */
  .blog-stories__media img {
    transform-origin: var(--story-x, 50%) var(--story-y, 50%);
    transition: transform 0.9s var(--ease-out);
  }

  @media (hover: hover) and (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .blog-stories__card:hover .blog-stories__media img {
      transform: scale(var(--story-zoom, 1.12));
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .blog-stories__card:has(.blog-stories__link:focus-visible) .blog-stories__media img {
      transform: scale(var(--story-zoom, 1.12));
    }
  }

  .blog-stories__media::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(0deg, #000000d9 0%, #00000066 45%, #00000000 75%);
  }

  .blog-stories__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 1rem + 1vw, 2.25rem);
  }

  .blog-stories__category {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: var(--font-size-small);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* Figma: "Featured Story" in a dark glass pill with a thin light edge */
  .blog-stories__pill {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-sm);
    padding: 0.35em 1.25em;
    border: 1px solid #ffffff4d;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background-color: #ffffff1f;
    font-size: var(--font-size-body-sm);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-frost));
    backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-frost));
    box-shadow: var(--glass-rim);
  }

  .blog-stories__title {
    margin: 0;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: var(--font-size-h3);
  }

  /*
    Featured shape (the first card unless a Story block chooses otherwise): bigger title, pill and
    excerpt. Other shapes don't show a pill or an excerpt; a featured card hides the category when it
    has a pill (Figma). Landscape gets a medium title.
  */
  .blog-stories__card--featured .blog-stories__title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-h1);
  }

  .blog-stories__card--landscape .blog-stories__title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-h2);
  }

  .blog-stories__card:not(.blog-stories__card--featured) :is(.blog-stories__pill, .blog-stories__excerpt),
  .blog-stories__card--featured:has(.blog-stories__pill) .blog-stories__category {
    display: none;
  }

  .blog-stories__excerpt {
    margin: var(--space-sm) 0 0;
    color: #ffffffd9;
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
  }

  /*
    Featured title H2 in equal columns (the card is narrower) and on phones; smaller excerpt on phones.
    These rules come after the base rules above (same specificity: the later rule wins).
  */
  .blog-stories__grid--equal .blog-stories__card--featured .blog-stories__title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-h2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .blog-stories__card--featured .blog-stories__title {
      font-size: var(--font-size-h2);
    }

    .blog-stories__excerpt {
      font-size: var(--font-size-body-sm);
    }
  }

  /* The title's link covers the whole card: one click target, one tab stop per story */
  .blog-stories__link {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .blog-stories__link::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
  }

  /*
    Focus ring on the whole card, in the scheme accent (Highlight color if set). Only with :has();
    other browsers keep the link's own ring, so a keyboard user always sees where the focus is.
  */
  @supports selector(:has(*)) {
    .blog-stories__link:focus-visible {
      outline: none;
    }

    .blog-stories__card:has(.blog-stories__link:focus-visible) {
      outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
      outline-offset: 4px;
    }
  }

  /*
    Entrance ("Scroll animation" setting): the grid only triggers (it stays visible); its cards start
    moved and transparent, then glide in one after another (0.12s apart, capped so a long list doesn't
    keep the last cards waiting) when the grid scrolls into view. The selectors repeat [data-animate]
    and :not(.is-visible) to outrank the theme's generic "hide until visible" rule in critical.css,
    which would otherwise move the whole mosaic as one block.
  */
  .blog-stories__grid[data-animate='fade-up'] { --story-from: translateY(2rem); }
  .blog-stories__grid[data-animate='zoom-in'] { --story-from: scale(0.94); }
  .blog-stories__grid[data-animate='slide-top'] { --story-from: translateY(-3rem); }
  .blog-stories__grid[data-animate='slide-bottom'] { --story-from: translateY(3rem); }
  .blog-stories__grid[data-animate='slide-left'] { --story-from: translateX(-4rem); }
  .blog-stories__grid[data-animate='slide-right'] { --story-from: translateX(4rem); }

  .blog-stories__card:nth-child(2) { --card-index: 1; }
  .blog-stories__card:nth-child(3) { --card-index: 2; }
  .blog-stories__card:nth-child(4) { --card-index: 3; }
  .blog-stories__card:nth-child(5) { --card-index: 4; }
  .blog-stories__card:nth-child(n + 6) { --card-index: 5; }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .js.animations-on .blog-stories__grid[data-animate],
    .js.animations-on .blog-stories__grid[data-animate]:not(.is-visible) {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
      transition: none;
    }

    .js.animations-on .blog-stories__grid[data-animate] .blog-stories__card {
      transition:
        opacity 0.8s var(--ease-out),
        transform 0.8s var(--ease-out);
      transition-delay: calc(var(--card-index, 0) * 0.12s);
    }

    .js.animations-on .blog-stories__grid[data-animate]:not(.is-visible) .blog-stories__card {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: var(--story-from, none);
    }
  }

  /*
    Theme editor preview: while a Story block is selected (script below), its card stays zoomed in and
    a dot marks the zoom point, so the merchant sees the effect of Zoom amount / Zoom towards straight
    away instead of having to hover. Only in the editor; the live store never gets the class.
  */
  .blog-stories__card.is-zoom-preview .blog-stories__media img {
    transform: scale(var(--story-zoom, 1.12));
  }

  .blog-stories__card.is-zoom-preview .blog-stories__media::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: var(--story-y, 50%);
    inset-inline-start: var(--story-x, 50%);
    z-index: 1;
    inline-size: 1.25rem;
    block-size: 1.25rem;
    border: 3px solid #ffffff;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px #00000059, 0 2px 8px #00000066;
    translate: -50% -50%;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
  /**
   * Theme editor only: while a Story block is selected, keep its card zoomed in with a dot on the zoom
   * point (class is-zoom-preview), so Zoom amount / Zoom towards can be judged without hovering.
   * The editor sends shopify:block:select / shopify:block:deselect to the block's element (the card,
   * which carries block.shopify_attributes), including after a setting change re-renders the section.
   * The listeners sit on document and are added one time (the flag), so a re-rendered or moved section
   * adds nothing: no AbortController is needed.
   */
  if (window.Shopify?.designMode && !window.oroskinStoryPreview) {
    window.oroskinStoryPreview = true;
    const toggle = (event, on) => {
      const card = event.target.closest?.('.blog-stories__card');
      if (card) card.classList.toggle('is-zoom-preview', on);
    };
    document.addEventListener('shopify:block:select', (event) => toggle(event, true));
    document.addEventListener('shopify:block:deselect', (event) => toggle(event, false));
  }
{% endjavascript %}

